    "phrases": [
      "Urns began arriving",
      "at a German",
      "prisoner-of-war camp.",
      "They held the ashes of Allied",
      "airmen who had escaped",
      "through a tunnel dug",
      "under the camp fence.",
      "The German government",
      "said the men had been shot",
      "resisting capture or trying",
      "to escape again.",
      "Police offices in different",
      "parts of the country sent",
      "Berlin reports on separate",
      "shootings, all giving",
      "the same explanation.",
      "The accounts matched",
      "so closely that Berlin",
      "ordered them rewritten.",
      "Fifty of the men who made",
      "it through that tunnel",
      "were killed.",
      "The escape began",
      "on the night of March 24,",
      "1944, at Stalag Luft Three,",
      "a German camp for captured",
      "Allied airmen.",
      "The prisoners",
      "had been digging",
      "in secret for months.",
      "They used boards",
      "from their beds",
      "to hold up the tunnel walls.",
      "Empty milk tins became",
      "pipes for pumping",
      "air underground.",
      "About two hundred men",
      "were supposed to get",
      "out that night.",
      "Then the first man",
      "came up through the exit",
      "and found that the tunnel",
      "stopped short of the woods.",
      "Anyone who came",
      "out had open ground to cross,",
      "within sight of the camp.",
      "The prisoners used a rope",
      "to signal back to the tunnel",
      "when the way was clear.",
      "By the time the guards",
      "stopped the escape,",
      "seventy-six men had got out.",
      "Only three made it to safety.",
      "The other seventy-three",
      "were recaptured,",
      "and for some of the men",
      "in custody,",
      "the next trip would be in a car",
      "with the Gestapo,",
      "the Nazi secret police.",
      "Hitler ordered",
      "the execution of dozens",
      "of the recaptured men.",
      "Instructions went",
      "out from Berlin",
      "to local police offices.",
      "The police were to turn",
      "over selected prisoners",
      "to the Gestapo,",
      "supposedly for questioning.",
      "The instructions also gave",
      "the story the officers",
      "were to tell afterward.",
      "The prisoners had been shot",
      "trying to get away.",
      "Some of the men",
      "who were eventually sent",
      "back to camp had seen what",
      "happened in one of the jails.",
      "Officials picked men",
      "out from their cells.",
      "The men selected were led",
      "away in handcuffs and driven",
      "off under armed guard.",
      "The prisoners who returned",
      "to camp lived to tell",
      "the British what they’d seen.",
      "The Gestapo took prisoners",
      "out in small groups and killed",
      "them at different locations.",
      "The bodies were cremated.",
      "Urns were sent back",
      "to the camp,",
      "and reports went to Berlin.",
      "After Britain made",
      "the deaths public,",
      "Berlin told the local offices",
      "to rewrite their accounts.",
      "Swiss representatives",
      "who monitored",
      "the treatment of prisoners",
      "of war were expected",
      "to ask for details.",
      "After the war, investigators",
      "from Britain’s",
      "Royal Air Force went",
      "looking for the men who’d",
      "carried out the killings.",
      "One case took them back",
      "to the spring of 1944,",
      "when two cars left a town",
      "near the Danish border.",
      "They were carrying",
      "four recaptured airmen.",
      "One was James Catanach,",
      "an Australian pilot who’d",
      "made it through the tunnel.",
      "He was the only prisoner",
      "in the first car.",
      "The other three",
      "were in the second.",
      "The drivers had orders",
      "to keep the road",
      "clear of passersby.",
      "Catanach’s car got there first.",
      "He was taken through a gate",
      "into a field and shot.",
      "When the second car arrived,",
      "the three men were led",
      "into the same field and killed.",
      "The drivers",
      "stayed by their cars.",
      "Later, when the report",
      "had to be rewritten,",
      "the officers proposed",
      "a new version.",
      "It said the two",
      "drivers had each shot",
      "a prisoner who tried to run.",
      "Both drivers refused to sign.",
      "Their commander sent",
      "a revised report",
      "to Berlin anyway.",
      "After the war, two other men",
      "who’d been there admitted",
      "firing at the prisoners.",
      "The men involved",
      "disagreed about who’d",
      "fired some of the shots.",
      "At the trial, the question",
      "would be what each of them",
      "had done, from giving",
      "the orders to driving the cars.",
      "In 1947,",
      "eighteen men faced a British",
      "military court in Hamburg.",
      "One was Max Wielen,",
      "the head of the criminal",
      "police in the region",
      "where the camp stood.",
      "He’d helped direct the search",
      "after the escape.",
      "The court heard that he’d",
      "been shown the killing",
      "order before prisoners",
      "in his region were handed",
      "over to the Gestapo.",
      "Wielen alone was convicted",
      "on the charges covering",
      "the wider killing operation.",
      "He was sentenced",
      "to life in prison.",
      "The other seventeen",
      "were convicted for their roles",
      "in specific murders.",
      "The two drivers",
      "argued that they’d",
      "only driven the cars.",
      "The question",
      "for the court was whether",
      "they had knowingly",
      "helped carry out the killings",
      "by bringing the prisoners",
      "to that field.",
      "Both drivers were convicted",
      "and sentenced",
      "to ten years in prison.",
      "While the war was still going",
      "on, the urns had been placed",
      "in a",
      "stone memorial in the woods",
      "outside the camp.",
      "The prisoners tended",
      "it for as long",
      "as they remained",
      "at Stalag Luft Three."
    ]
  }
}
